For a tree-decomposition $(T_0,\cdots,T_{k-1})$ of an edge-labeled graph, define its \emph{signature} $v^{(T_0,\dots,T_{k-1})}$ by
  \begin{align} v^{(T_0,\dots,T_{k-1})}\coloneqq \sum_{i=0}^{k-1} i\cdot v^{T_i}.
  \end{align}

Let $t=4$, and $k=2$.
  Below, $H$ is a $2$-weakly-partition-connected hypergraph.
  We take a tree assignment of $H$ to obtain an edge-labeled graph $G$ on 6 edges, where each edge is labeled by its color.
  The tree-decomposition $T_0\cup T_1$ demonstrates that $G$ is 2-distinguishable:
